--- OUT --->
0
drop
--- AST --->
// the wrapper scope holds the header declaration and then the loop. the loop itself carries no init,
// which is the whole reason `$i`'s lifetime needs no rule of its own - it is an ordinary frame local,
// and a `break` or a `return` out of the body unwinds it through the machinery a block already has
CHECK: vardecl<type<int32>>($i) = literal<int32>(0)
CHECK: for (; binexp<bool>(varref<int32>(var($i)) < literal<int32>(1)); varref<int32>(var($i)) = binexp<int32>(varref<int32>(var($i)) + literal<int32>(1)))

--- RAST --->
// and the body's own local is dropped at the end of the body, once per iteration. the `for` survives to
// codegen - unlike `foreach` it is not a transient node, so `-ar` still shows one
CHECK: for (;
CHECK: vardecl<type<Noisy>>($n)
CHECK: call destructor(addrof<Noisy&>(varref<Noisy>(var($n)))): void
